# Production deployment

Production server: `139.59.139.30` — project path `/var/www/mayode-system`.

## Required workflow

1. **Commit and push** all changes to GitHub (`origin/main` or the agreed branch).
2. **On production**, pull from GitHub, then build/restart services as needed.

```bash
# On production (SSH)
cd /var/www/mayode-system
git pull origin main
cd backend && npm install && npx nest build && pm2 restart mayode-api
# web/mobile only if those changed on production
```

## Never do this

- Do **not** use `scp`, `rsync`, or manual file copies to deploy code to production.
- Do **not** edit source files directly on the production server (except `.env` and runtime config).
- Do **not** run seed scripts on production unless the user explicitly asks.

## Database seeds

Seed scripts (`backend/prisma/seed-*.ts`) run on production only when the user requests it, still via git pull — not by copying a single file with `scp`.

## Mobile / Expo

Mobile dev uses Metro locally; production API is `http://139.59.139.30:3002/api/v1`. Backend deploys follow the GitHub pull workflow above.
